d of course federica mogherini for  having organized this event and brought  against bringing us together here today  thank you thank you well I joined my  voice to the Chancellor's one in  thanking our Asian partners in  particular the two ministers that are  with us but also the other delegations  in total European and Asian delegations  of 53 which gives you the magnitude of  these two days with over 40 delegations  represented either at level of heads of  state and government or ministerial  level I think it is the azzam summit the  summit between Asia and Europe and the  highest political level in for sure in  recent years and this tells you the  importance we both attach to this  partnership and definitely out of these  two days of work we come with reinforced  global partnership between Europe and  Asia what we agree together matters not  only to the two of us but also to the  entire world you know the numbers Europe  and Asia together are 55 percent of  global trade 60 percent of global  population 65 percent of global economy  75% of global tourism and if we continue  in the list you realize that together  represent a real global power and this  summit has allowed us to translate this  global weight that we share into  concrete policy initiatives that can  make a real difference for the world the  transfer is already mentioned three key  areas for intense cooperation on climate  change action on free and fair trade and  on digital I would like to mention a  couple of more points that were at the  centre of our work for sure our common  work on security and the issues that are  on top of our foreign policy agendas  strengthening cooperation between us on  international and regional security if  we see developments in our regions both  in Asia and in Europe we see the need to  protect and promote rules-based  international order not only on trade  but also in security and a cooperative  approach to foreign policy in particular  we discussed our full support and our  willingness to accompany the diplomatic  process in the Korean Peninsula in this  respect I would like to commend and  appreciate the leadership of the  Republic of Korea president moon foreign  minister conch that have indeed put a  new hope not only in the Korean  Peninsula not only in Asia but in the  entire world and we are committed  together Europe and Asia to make these  negotiations a success and to accompany  them in the best possible manner  we also share the intention to uphold  the multilateral system with the United  Nations and its core all other  multilateral multilateral nuclear  non-proliferation agreements starting  from the jcpoa and another point we  discussed at length with a lot of  understanding and convergences is the  need to increase connectivity between  our two continents just last Monday a  few days ago the European Union foreign  ministers agreed on ways to strengthen  connectivity between Europe and Asia in  a sustainable comprehensive and  rules-based manner and I'm happy to see  that this approach is also shared by our  Asian partners so indeed we have decided  to use all the potential for bringing  Asia and Europe closer together not only  on the level of transport and  infrastructures but also on digital and  economic links as the Chancellor said  there is a clear commitment between us  to maintain and strengthen open free  trade to work for the reform of WTO  later this afternoon in a few hours  we'll design a new partnership free  trade and investment agreement with  Singapore only a few months after we  sign important agreements with Japan and  others are in the making so there is I  would say a new wave of  agreements trade agreements but also  partnership agreements the European  Union is promoting around the world and  in the asia-pacific region in particular  let me conclude by saying that the  summit was accompanied by many important  side events that reported to us the  results of their work civil society  business