sue very seriously but  having said all of that the potential of  the fourth Industrial Revolution and all  the technology that it it implies has  great potential and we all need to work  towards the the benefits and and to  mitigate the negative consequences of  that thirdly the connectivity between  Europe and ASEAN is something that we  are also very keenly involved and being  one of the most wired countries in the  world with IT sector that is  particularly enhanced we're ready to  contribute to enhancing and  strengthening the connectivity within  our regions but also across Europe and  Asia we of course had this opportunity  to brief their leaders on the  developments on the Korean Peninsula  and thank you frederica you've always  been a solid supporter behind all of our  diplomatic initiatives in this regard  but at the end we have a very different  situation on the Korean Peninsula from  where we were one year ago where we were  faced with continued North Korean  provocations and an even talk of a  potential for military clash to today  where we are solidly on the road to a  peaceful diplomatic resolution of North  Korea's nuclear missile challenge  coupled with a new phase in South North  Korean relations toward a dialogue and  reconciliation three South North Korean  summits one us North Korea's summit and  more in the making and so definitely we  are in a very change situation on the  Korean Peninsula and this would not have  happened without the support that we  have received from mood Frederika and  her team and certainly the members of  the the European Union as well so  and this was a wonderful opportunity for  us to brief and to assure the leaders  here that we are definitely on the right  track if we stay this course we get  denuclearization we get permanent peace  on the Korean Peninsula we will get  connectivity between Europe and Asia  even further strengthened as well  because once you have North Korea as  part of the normal economic activity on