yed with the UK  part of the European Union the UK is our  second largest trading partner in the  European Union under the FTA that's been  very beneficial to both sides and I  think I can safely say that on both  sides the UK and us were very keen to  maintain that level of collaboration  obviously this requires a lot of work a  lot of contingency planning if I may put  it that way but within our own  government but in collaboration with our  counterparts in the UK we are already  having serious discussions about this  and my president had an excellent  discussion with Prime Minister made  today thank you if I can if I can remind  us all though that as long as the UK is  part of the European Union they cannot  negotiate nor conclude any additional to  any separate trade agreements and this  includes the transition periods for us  to be all aware of what we're talking  about with this I have to conclude this  press conference but thank you very much  for coming and there is also ample  material available including the chairs  statement
 

